  "question": {
    "text": "If two parabolas <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>–</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>–</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> have only one common point <math><mi>P</mi></math>, then the equation of normal to <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>–</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> at <math><mi>P</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
